From: GLM-EXL3-2x-GB10 testing line <tensorfold-zig-testing@local>
Subject: glm-warmturns: the fork 0104 port — a user message after an agent loop resumes past the loop's turns

PROVENANCE: ported from MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-DGX-Sparks-1104's engine
patch 0104 (Apache-2.0, (c) MiaAI Lab), against our v1.2.5 + the 17-patch
stack tree (4b8d7c91...), 2026-11-09, by this line. GLM's template renders
an assistant turn's reasoning only after the last user message
(clear_thinking), so during an agent loop every turn carries its reasoning
and the next user message re-prefills the whole loop (50-100K tokens, 10-30
s). The server's warm.zig already prefills the next turn's prompt in the
background after a reply — the GLM family never declared warm_turns.

WHAT THE PORT CARRIES: the family declares warm_quiet (150 ms, Nemotron's);
the chunk gate's cancel check reads the stream's yield check so a warm pass
steps aside once real work waits (keeping the states it reached); the lane
host's quiet() waits on warmBlocked (the fill-queue case the v1.2.5
mainline carried in warmBlocked but never called from quiet()); setup ends
a stepped-aside pass visibly; warm.zig's dummy next turn is a TOOL message
after a tool-call reply (a user-turn rendering would re-prefill the cleared
loop on every tool call); the Host carries warm_quiet and the startup phase
wires it (ADAPTED: our tree wires it in cuda_startup_phase.zig — v1.2.5
moved the startup phases there — not inline in openWith as the fork's).

THE KNOB: TF_GLM_WARM_TURNS=0 turns the warm pass off (the A/B kill
switch; the default on) — applied at the wiring (cuda_startup_phase.zig,
runtime getenv in this file's idiom; a container-level const cannot call
getenv at comptime, the first switch form's compile error).

FIDELITY: 104/104 fork + lines verbatim in the ported tree, with the two
documented file-path adaptations (the quiet wiring lives in
cuda_startup_phase.zig; the lane_host_warm_test import rides our tree's
existing wiring). The tool-parse host suite: PASS on the final tree;
compile RC=0 (fatbins + native, sm_121) receipted on the final tree.

STATUS: STAGED for the warmturnsqual A/B battery (the off arm runs
TF_GLM_WARM_TURNS=0): the fork's measured shape is ours to confirm — the
next user message after a tool loop resumes past the loop (their 9.3K loop
cached 8,192 of its tokens vs 4,096 before; 1.6 s to answer vs 3.5 s), the
§2 gates PASS, hardmode 95, the vision 4/4, the greedy same-bits sha holds.
Adoption moves config.sh's PATCHES + the promoted repo's.

