 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20a=20user=20message=20after=20an=20agent=20loop=20re?=
 =?UTF-8?q?sumes=20past=20the=20loop's=20turns?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

THE PORT: Mia 1104's engine patch 0104, against the v1.2.5 + the 17-patch
stack tree (4b8d7c91...). GLM's template renders an assistant turn's
reasoning only after the last user message (clear_thinking), so during an
agent loop every turn carries its reasoning and the next user message
re-prefills the whole loop (50-100K tokens, 10-30 s). The server's
warm.zig already prefills the next turn's prompt in the background after a
reply — the GLM family just never declared warm_turns.

- families/glm/cuda_native.zig declares warm_quiet (150 ms, Nemotron's).
- families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig: the chunk gate's cancel check also reads
  the stream's yield check (s.yields()), so a warm pass steps aside at its
  next chunk gate once a request waits or a stream decodes, keeping the
  states it reached.
- native/cuda.zig: the Host carries warm_quiet (the family's value); the
  startup phase wires h.warm_quiet, not nemotron's constant. ADAPTED: our
  tree wires warm_quiet in cuda_startup_phase.zig (v1.2.5 moved the
  startup phases there), not inline in openWith.
- core/lane_host.zig: setup ends a stepped-aside pass visibly
  (h.remove + h.finish(.cancelled, "other work came first")), not the
  silent ended() stub.
- server/warm.zig: after a reply WITH tool calls the dummy next turn is a
  TOOL message (the next message is a tool result, not a user message); a
  template that clears earlier turns' reasoning renders the loop
  differently before each, and a user-turn rendering after a call would
  prefill the cleared loop on every tool call. After an answer the dummy
  turn stays a user message. (applied from the patch verbatim)
- the tests: lane_host_warm_test's stepped-aside case + late_system_test's
  warm-channel case (applied from the patch verbatim).

The tree this commit produces is the v125 verified tree + this port only.
The tool-parse host suite: PASS (the warm tests ride the module graph).
compile RC=0: receipted separately.
